      "content": "i tried checking the securityContext and the volumes, and everything seems to align with the dev env. i even ran a debug pod with the same mount config and it didn't crash. \n\nit's super weird because it's like these files just vanish as soon as it hits the production cluster. could this be a race condition with the container runtime or maybe some weird behavior with how GKE handles the node local storage? im starting to feel like im chasing ghosts here. any idea what else could cause such a random failure?",
